# False positives confirmed via manual investigation (see README, Milestone 1
# security notes). Trivy's "sbom" analyzer duplicate-detects a stale package
# record for these two libraries alongside the real, correctly-patched
# filesystem package (confirmed via "python-pkg" analyzer + FilePath pointing
# at the actual dist-info METADATA). Source of the stale "sbom" record is
# unidentified (same image layer, no FilePath) -- likely related to
# https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy/discussions/10093 (PEP 770 SBOM
# duplicate-detection), not yet fully covering this case in the Trivy version
# used here.
#
# msgpack: real installed version confirmed 1.2.1 (fixed); stale sbom record says 1.1.2
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
# setuptools: real installed version confirmed 83.0.0 (fixed); stale sbom record says 70.3.0
